# gitignore-syntax exclusions for Workload API source upload (see
# docs/agent/deployment-runtimes.md).
#
# Read by `artifact_code.py` in the agent's `*_workload_api` package (a
# top-level package in the Pulumi project) when Pulumi archives and uploads
# agent source for the C2W scenario with a platform-generated Dockerfile.
# The replace-on-change hash is computed from the same archived bytes, so this
# file is the single source of truth for what counts as agent source.
tests/
*.coverage
.DS_Store
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.uv/
docker_context/
docker_context.tar.gz
.env
.env.*
model-metadata.yaml
.wapiignore
